  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "Doctors thought the smoke would warm the body and wake it up. It didn't. The kits also had tools for blowing air into the lungs, which was actually a decent idea. By the 1810s, experiments showed tobacco is bad for the heart, and the idea faded.",
