  {
   "who": "N",
   "say": "His doctors followed the best medicine of their day: drain blood to fight the illness. Remember Benjamin Rush and his thunderclappers? He was one of bleeding's biggest fans. Over about twelve hours, Washington's doctors bled him four times.",
   "show": {
    "k": "scene",
    "bg": "library",
